---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---
<LegalPage title="Privacy policy" description="How Advica AI Solutions Ltd collects, uses and protects your personal data under UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018." updated="26 October 2026">
  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {site.legalName} (“we”, “us”) is a company registered in {site.registeredIn}{site.companyNumber && <> (company number {site.companyNumber})</>}, with its registered office at {site.address.street}, {site.address.town}, {site.address.postcode}.
    We are the data controller for the personal data described in this policy and are registered with the UK Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO){site.icoNumber && <> under registration number {site.icoNumber}</>}.
  </p>
  <p>This policy explains how we handle personal data in line with the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR) and the Data Protection Act 2018.</p>

  <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Enquiries:</strong> your name, email address, company, phone number and anything you tell us about your project when you use our contact form, project cost estimator or AI readiness quiz, email us or call us.</li>
    <li><strong>Clients:</strong> business contact details and correspondence needed to plan and deliver our services.</li>
    <li><strong>Website use:</strong> our website does not use cookies or tracking for advertising. Our hosting provider keeps short-term technical logs (such as IP address and browser type) for security and to keep the site running. If we use website analytics, we only use privacy-friendly tools that do not use cookies or identify individual visitors.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. How we use it and why</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To reply to your enquiry and discuss your project — because you asked us to (taking steps before entering a contract) and our legitimate interest in responding to business enquiries.</li>
    <li>To deliver services to clients — to perform our contract with you.</li>
    <li>To keep business and tax records — to comply with our legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not use your information for unsolicited marketing, and we never sell it.</p>

  <h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We only share personal data where needed, with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Service providers</strong> who help us run our business, such as our website and form host (Netlify), our email provider and our call-booking tool.</li>
    <li><strong>Our engineering delivery partner</strong>, where needed to scope or deliver your project, under confidentiality and data-handling obligations.</li>
    <li><strong>Finance providers</strong>, only if you ask us to introduce you to monthly financing.</li>
    <li><strong>Professional advisers</strong> (such as lawyers and accountants), and authorities where the law requires it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. International transfers</h2>
  <p>Some of these organisations may process data outside the UK. When that happens we make sure appropriate safeguards are in place, such as UK adequacy regulations or the ICO’s International Data Transfer Agreement (IDTA) or Addendum.</p>

  <h2>6. Keeping your data secure</h2>
  <p>We use appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect personal data, including restricting access to people who need it and encrypting data in transit.</p>

  <h2>7. How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>We keep personal data only for as long as we need it for the purposes above. Enquiry details that don’t lead to a project are deleted when no longer needed. Client records are kept for as long as required for legal, tax and accounting purposes.</p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right to access, correct or delete your personal data, to restrict or object to how we use it, and to data portability. To use any of these rights, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
  <p>If you’re unhappy with how we’ve handled your data, please tell us first. You also have the right to complain to the ICO at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.</p>

  <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The latest version will always be on this page.</p>
</LegalPage>
